Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 20:05:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(db): exclude internal pg_* schemas from explorer tree

The schema explorer leaked `pg_toast` (and other `pg_*` internal
schemas) as non-expandable dead-end nodes because the schema filter
only excluded `pg_catalog` and `information_schema`. Switch to a
`not like 'pg\_%'` filter so all internal schemas are excluded, leaving
only user schemas (public, app, ...) that actually expand.

Add live introspection tests (schemas/relations/columns) and a live
panel test that drives lazy expansion connection -> schema -> relation
-> columns against a real Postgres, plus the test-support dev-deps and
gpui_tokio/allow_parking setup the existing connect_and_select test was
missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GbHBSdw2MBBgxKxLnVCbf6
